content:
All three spec updates are in place and parse cleanly.

```json
{
    "specs_updated": [
        {
            "spec_name": "server",
            "change_description": "Modified the `ws.py` bullet of the Server Modules requirement to describe the narrowed MSG_HISTORY_DATA broadcast-suppression boundary: the /ws/ui broadcast is suppressed only for a `mode: full` response that resolves a pending REST pull waiter (`suppress_broadcast = resolved_pull and mode == protocol.HISTORY_MODE_FULL`); a `mode: append` real-time increment is ALWAYS broadcast even when it also resolves a waiter, so respond/interject increments keep appending in already-subscribed live views, with the REST-pull-initiating client deduplicating via frontend `dedupeAppendRecords`. Fixes symptom A."
        },
        {
            "spec_name": "daemon",
            "change_description": "Updated the `history.py` bullet of the Daemon Modules requirement in two places: (1) refined the un-terminated-trailing-line rule in read_flow's byte-offset reader to branch on JSON parseability — a complete record without a trailing newline (terminal-written and *.jsonl.from-<branch> sidecar files) is consumed and advances the offset, while a mid-write truncated tail is left intact for re-read, identifying this as the root cause of the worktree first-assistant-body-empty symptom; (2) added project_root preservation across the worktree read path — read_active_flows' final-flush calls read_flow with each flow's own project_root via a root_by_flow map, _resolve_flow_dir resolves worktree session history directories, and respond/interject (client.py / _resolve_interject_root) preserves the same root. Fixes symptom B."
        },
        {
            "spec_name": "running-flow-console",
            "change_description": "Added a new scenario 'Live append after respond/interject keeps appending without re-entering the view' to the Live-Append Record Deduplication Against Snapshot requirement, locking the front/back-end contract that after respond/interject the server keeps broadcasting mode:append increments (even when a frame also serves a REST pull) and the frontend dedupeAppendRecords renders each record exactly once with no record lost and no view re-entry needed. Verifies symptom A acceptance."
        }
    ],
    "new_capabilities": [],
    "spec_decisions": [],
    "notes": "All changes were directed modifications to existing Requirements (two modify_requirement, one add_scenario) — no new Requirements were created, so spec_decisions is empty. The pre-existing 'Worktree merge-back sidecar files' paragraph in daemon::Daemon Modules already covered sidecar enumeration and logical-step merging, so I only added the missing project_root preservation and trailing-line parseability details rather than duplicating. Note: both server::Server Modules and daemon::Daemon Modules continue to emit the renderer's 'should be split into smaller items' advisory (they exceed the byte threshold and are multi-bullet module registries); per the Spec Split Criteria this is a recommendation for `se3 sync` to handle, not for update_spec to split."
}
```

